Steps:
1. Send a POST request to /api/auth/signin with the payload in testData. 2. Verify the response status and body.

Test Data: {
  "username": "owner@shop.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

Expected Result:
HTTP 200 OK response with a JSON body containing: {
  "status": "success",
  "message": "User signed in successfully",
  "data": {
    "id": <non-null number>,
    "username": "owner@shop.com",
    "email": "owner@shop.com",
    "roles": ["ROLE_OWNER"],
    "shopId": 1,
    "areaId": 5
  }
}

Steps:
1. Send a POST request to /api/auth/login with the payload in testData. 2. Verify the response status and body.

Test Data: {
  "username": "owner@shop.com",
  "pin": "1234"
}

Expected Result:
HTTP 200 OK response with a JSON body containing: {
  "status": "success",
  "message": "User logged in successfully",
  "data": {
    "id": <non-null number>,
    "username": "owner@shop.com",
    "email": "owner@shop.com",
    "roles": ["ROLE_OWNER"],
    "shopId": 1,
    "areaId": 5
  }
}

